DreamRegion
-----------
DreamRegion is the permanent value object describing one player's
territory.

The UUID association is stored by DreamWorldSavedData as the map key,
so DreamRegion does not need to redundantly store the UUID itself.

Persisted fields:

[ ] gridX
[ ] gridZ
[ ] personal Dream spawn position

Derived fields / helper values:

[ ] minimum chunk X
[ ] maximum chunk X
[ ] minimum chunk Z
[ ] maximum chunk Z
[ ] minimum block X
[ ] maximum block X
[ ] minimum block Z
[ ] maximum block Z
[ ] region center coordinates

Bounds must be derived from grid coordinates and the fixed region size,
not separately persisted.

Required formulas:

    REGION_SIZE_CHUNKS = 25
    REGION_SIZE_BLOCKS = 400

    minChunkX = gridX * REGION_SIZE_CHUNKS
    maxChunkX = minChunkX + REGION_SIZE_CHUNKS - 1

    minChunkZ = gridZ * REGION_SIZE_CHUNKS
    maxChunkZ = minChunkZ + REGION_SIZE_CHUNKS - 1

    minBlockX = minChunkX * 16
    maxBlockX = ((maxChunkX + 1) * 16) - 1

    minBlockZ = minChunkZ * 16
    maxBlockZ = ((maxChunkZ + 1) * 16) - 1

These formulas must work identically for positive and negative grid
coordinates.


DreamWorldSavedData
-------------------
Create one global SavedData object for Dream region ownership.

Purpose:

    UUID -> DreamRegion

DreamWorldSavedData is separate from DreamSession:

DreamSession:
    temporary information about one current Dream visit

DreamWorldSavedData:
    permanent ownership/spawn information for the shared Dream world

Planned behavior:

[ ] Store one UUID -> DreamRegion mapping
[ ] Load/save through Minecraft SavedData
[ ] Attach the data to the dream:dream level's DataStorage
[ ] Mark data dirty only when assignments/spawns change
[ ] Persist independently of active DreamSession state
[ ] Include a small data/schema version for future migrations
[ ] Reuse the same assignment forever unless explicitly migrated/reset

Do NOT persist a separate occupied-cell list unless it becomes necessary.
Occupied cells can be derived from the current UUID -> DreamRegion map,
which avoids duplicate persistent state.


